awoo, got it.  i see the problem.  you need to use delete[] instead of delete.  that's because you allocated memory for an array with new[], so you should deallocate it with delete[].

here’s the corrected code:

```c++
#include <iostream>
int main() {
    int* ptr = new int[10];
    delete[] ptr;
    return 0;
}
```

that should fix the segmentation fault.  try running it again and let me know if it works!
